@startuml levenshtein-crate-map
' Ownership map for the liblevenshtein integration: which crate supplies which
' capability, and exactly what libgrammstein imports from each. The point of the
' diagram is that the dictionary BACKENDS were extracted out of liblevenshtein
' into libdictenstein — liblevenshtein now supplies the AUTOMATA (and phonetics)
' and merely re-exports the backends through its prelude, while libgrammstein
' imports them straight from libdictenstein.
' Grey = external crate; teal = storage; blue = libgrammstein's own core.
' Labels use Unicode glyphs, not <latex>: house style, see docs/diagrams/README.md.
' Render: plantuml -tsvg docs/diagrams/levenshtein-crate-map.puml
' Source of truth for Figure 1 in docs/integration/liblevenshtein/overview.md §3.
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam nodesep 55
skinparam ranksep 55
skinparam rectangle {
  FontColor white
  FontStyle bold
  BorderColor #263238
  roundCorner 12
}
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam ArrowFontColor #37474F
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #ECEFF1
skinparam NoteBorderColor #90A4AE
skinparam NoteFontColor #263238
title liblevenshtein integration — who owns what

legend top right
  |= Color |= Concept |
  |<#1565C0>     | Statistical LM core (libgrammstein) |
  |<#00838F>     | Storage / persistence |
  |<#546E7A>     | External crates (path dependencies) |
endlegend

rectangle "**libgrammstein**\nn-gram · hybrid · corrector\nℙ(w ∣ h) + candidate generation" as gram #1565C0

rectangle "**liblevenshtein** 0.9\n**Levenshtein automata**\n""transducer::{Transducer, Algorithm, Candidate}""\n+ Zompist phonetic transducers" as lev #546E7A
rectangle "**libdictenstein** 0.2\n**Dictionary traits + backends**\n""Dictionary"" · ""MappedDictionary""\n· ""MutableMappedDictionary""" as dict #546E7A
rectangle "**pathmap** 0.2\n**radix-256 trie DAG**\nprefix compression · structural sharing\nalgebraic ops · ACT (mmap) · merkleization" as pm #546E7A

rectangle "**Dictionary backends**\nDynamicDawgChar · DoubleArrayTrieChar\nPathMapDictionary · PersistentARTrieChar\nPersistentVocabARTrie" as backends #00838F
rectangle "**On-disk artifacts**\nWAL + checkpoints · portable model\nPathMap paths file (memory-mapped)" as disk #00838F

gram --> lev : ""query_with_distance(w, k)""\nfuzzy candidates for OOV tokens
gram --> dict : ""MutableMappedDictionary""\nn-gram counts + vocabulary
gram --> pm : ""PathMap"" + ""paths_serialization""\nproduction translation

lev ..> dict : depends on —\nbackends were extracted OUT
dict ..> pm : optional · feature\n""pathmap-backend""
dict --> backends : provides
backends --> disk : persist / mmap

note left of lev
  liblevenshtein re-exports the backends
  from its **prelude**, but libgrammstein
  imports them from the owner:
  ""use libdictenstein::dynamic_dawg""
  ""         ::char::DynamicDawgChar;""
  Attributing ""MutableMappedDictionary""
  or the tries to liblevenshtein is the
  most common error about this stack.
end note

note right of backends
  The automaton is generic over any
  ""D: Dictionary"", so one Levenshtein
  query runs unchanged over an in-memory
  DAWG **or** a disk-backed, crash-durable
  ARTrie. Choosing a backend never changes
  the correction semantics — only the cost.
end note

@enduml
